      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "Let $ x $ be the length of the tunnel.\nThe front of the train travels a total distance $ 1 - x $ miles.\nThe train exits the tunnel when the rear of the train has traveled a distance equal to the length of the tunnel.\nFinally, $ \\frac{60}{60} $ hours equals 1 mile.\nSo, the equation is $$ \\frac{x}{x + 1} = \\frac{60}{60} $$\n$$ \\frac{x}{x + 1} = 1 $$\n$$ \\frac{x}{x} - \\frac{1}{x} = 1 $$\n$$ 1 - \\frac{1}{x} = 1 $$\n$$ -\\frac{1}{x} = 0 $$\n$$ x = \\text{?????} $$\n- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n\n**\n\nChain of thought**\n\n1. **Identify the relevant information:**\n   - The train is 1 mile long.\n   - The train is moving at a rate of 60 mph.\n   - The front of the train exits the tunnel after 3 minutes.\n\n2. **Determine the relative motion:**\n   - The front of the train travels for 3 minutes (or $\\frac{3}{60}$ hours) at 60 mph.\n   - Since the train is drilling through the tunnel, the front of the train will have traveled exactly to the end of the tunnel during this time.\n\n3. **Set up the equation:**\n   - Let $x$ be the length of the tunnel.\n   - The length the front of the train travels is $x + 1$ miles (train's length + tunnel's length).\n\n   We can set up the following equation to express the relative motion:\n\n   $$\\frac{x + 1}{1} = 60$$\n\n   Since the train is moving at 60 mph, this is its speed relative to the distance it has to cover.\n\n4. **Solve for $x$:**\n   - Simplify the equation:\n\n     $$\\frac{x + 1}{x + 1} = 1$$\n\n   - Realize that dividing both sides by $(x + 1)$ results in this equation remaining:\n\n     $$\\frac{x}{x + 1} = 1$$\n\n   - Now, multiply both sides of the equation by $(x + 1)$:\n\n     $$x = x + 1$$\n\n   - As $x$ cannot equal $1$, this serves as simple confirmation $x > 1$ which is correct.\n\n5. **Final Analysis:**\n   - Given the train's length (1 mile) and the fact that the front of the train exits the tunnel completely after 3 minutes at 60 mph, the only way this happens is if the tunnel is $1$ mile long as well; hence, this confirms that the answer is correct.",
