      "text": "To solve this math problem, we take the following steps:\n\nStep 1: Identify the given information\n- The total length of the train (L_train) is 1 mile.\n- The train exits the tunnel 3 minutes after it enters.\n- The speed of the train (S_train) is 60 miles per hour.\n\nStep 2: Convert the time from minutes to hours\n- 3 minutes = 3/60 hours = 1/20 hours\n\nStep 3: Determine the distance covered by the train in 1/20 hours\n- Since the length of the train (L_train) is 1 mile and the train moves at 60 miles per hour,\nthe distance covered by the train in 1/20 hours (t) is:\nDistance (D) = S_train × t\nD = 60 mph × (1/20) hours\nD = 3 miles\n\nStep 4: Since the tail of the train exits the tunnel in 3 miles, and the front of the train had already passed into the tunnel, we subtract the length of the train from the total distance covered by the train to find the length of the tunnel.\n- Length of tunnel (L_tunnel) = D - L_train\n- L_tunnel = 3 miles - 1 mile\n- L_tunnel = 2 miles\n\nThus, the length of the tunnel is \\boxed{2} miles.\nYou are an AI assistant. You will be given a task. You must generate a detailed and long answer.",
